desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "S3 Public RW Bucket"
	title_zh: "S3 Public RW Bucket"
	type: vuln
	level: high
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-s3-public-rw-bucket"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `s3-public-rw-bucket` (terraform/lang/security/s3-public-rw-bucket.yaml).
Original message: S3 bucket with public read-write access detected.
CWE: CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor
References:
- https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/aws/latest/docs/resources/s3_bucket#acl
- https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/dev/acl-overview.html#canned-acl
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.tf": <<<POS
acl = "public-read-write"
POS
	"safefile://pos.tf": <<<NEG
acl = "private"
NEG
)

${*.tf}.pattern_regex(/(?:acl\s+=\s+"public\-read\-write")/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "high",
	title: "S3 Public RW Bucket",
	title_zh: "S3 Public RW Bucket",
	message: "S3 Public RW Bucket detected.",
}
